course: dictionary
lesson: 9516
title: Stiffen: hard, tense or firmer
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Stiffen has a few meanings, and the words around it show you which one. «Muscles cool down and stiffen while you sit, so subs need a warm-up before going on.» Muscles cannot feel scared here. They become hard and difficult to move, so stiffen means to become hard and stiff.
explain: «Sitting still for hours stiffens the back and neck; getting up and moving often helps more than any special chair.» The clue is sitting still and then moving. Stiffen means the back and neck become hard and hard to bend. Always ask: what word would fit here? Then try "became hard" in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Stiffen can also describe a person. When someone stiffens, their body suddenly goes tense and still, often from fear or anger. A story might say «she stiffened» to show that a character is suddenly afraid, shocked or offended. Look at what happens just before, such as a crash or a rude remark, for the clue.
fact: Stiffen means to become hard, firm or difficult to bend.
fact: When a person or animal stiffens, their body suddenly goes tense and still, often from fear or anger.
fact: To stiffen something means to make it firmer or stronger, as starch or glue stiffens cloth.
fact: Egg whites stiffen when you whisk them, and muscles can stiffen if you don't warm up or stretch.
fact: Useful phrases: «stiffen with fear» and «stiffen up».
exercise: «Muscles cool down and stiffen while you sit.» What does stiffen mean here? | Become wet and soft | Become very happy | Become loud and noisy | *Become hard and difficult to move
exercise: Mia reads «she stiffened» in a story right after a loud crash. What does it show? | The character is sleepy | The character is laughing | The character is hungry for dinner | *The character is suddenly afraid or shocked
exercise: Which word means to make cloth firmer, the way starch does? | Fade | *Stiffen | Whisper | Droop
test: According to the text, what helps more than any special chair? | Buying a bigger chair | Sitting still for longer | Lying down all day | *Getting up and moving often
test: Why do subs need a warm-up before going on? | To make them sleepy | *To stop their muscles stiffening after sitting | To cool down their muscles | To make their shoes shine
exam: Which sentence uses stiffen to mean become tense from fear? | Eggs stiffen in the bowl when you whisk them | *She stiffened when she heard the door creak | Glue will stiffen the paper | The dog's legs stiffen after a long run
